    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test in the project, and the full `mvn test` build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `GOLD` membership tier rule so it satisfies the spec and the new `AcceptanceTest`.\n\n**What the rule requires:** `membershipTier` becomes `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (the DTOs, including `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum`, are generated from this spec) and updated its description to document the household rule.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 The base SILVER/BRONZE derivation lives in the stateless `OwnerMapper`, which can't see other owners. The GOLD upgrade needs the full owner set, so I added `applyHouseholdTier(...)` (with a `GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE = 3` constant) that counts owners sharing the owner's non-null `householdId` via `clinicService.findAllOwners()` and returns `GOLD` at 3+, else the base tier. It's applied on read in both `getOwner` and `addOwner`, mirroring how `bulkSignupWarning` is already enriched there. Because the new owner is saved before mapping, the third household member counts itself and reads back `GOLD`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Updated the `membershipTier` javadoc to note it derives only the base tier and that the GOLD upgrade is applied by the controller.\n\nThe GOLD override is a pure fall-through: owners with no `householdId` (the common case) keep their existing SILVER/BRONZE result unchanged.",
